---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ToolPage from "@bt/ui/ToolPage.astro";
import AdSlot from "@bt/ui/AdSlot.astro";
import WordCounter from "../../components/WordCounter.tsx";
---
<Layout
  bleed
  lang="en"
  title="Arabic word and character counter, remove diacritics | Baitaan"
  description="Count the words, characters, sentences and paragraphs in Arabic or English text, count the diacritics (tashkeel) and remove them in one click. Free, no sign-up."
>
  <ToolPage
    heading="Word and character counter"
    lead="Paste your text to see the number of words and characters, with and without spaces, and the number of diacritics. You can also strip all the diacritics in one click."
    updated="Updated: November 2026"
  >
    <WordCounter client:load lang="en" />

    <Fragment slot="guide">
      <h2>Why a counter built for Arabic?</h2>
      <p>Many counters treat diacritics (tashkeel) as letters, so vowelled Arabic text looks longer than it is. This tool shows the character count with and without diacritics, so you know the real length. It works for English text too.</p>

      <h2>Uses</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keeping to the word limit for articles, papers and assignments.</li>
        <li>Writing posts, product descriptions and ads of a set length.</li>
        <li>Removing diacritics before searching or pasting into systems that don't support them.</li>
      </ul>

      <AdSlot unit="0000000000" label="Advertisement" />

      <h2>How are sentences counted?</h2>
      <p>A sentence ends at each full stop, question mark (؟ or ?), exclamation mark or new line. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.</p>

      <h2>Example</h2>
      <p>The text: «الحمدُ للهِ ربِّ العالمين. هذه أداةٌ مجانيةٌ لعدِّ الكلمات.» (“Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. This is a free tool for counting words.”)</p>
      <ul class="ms-5 list-disc space-y-1">
        <li>Words: 9.</li>
        <li>Characters with spaces and diacritics: 59.</li>
        <li>Diacritics: 8, so 51 characters without them.</li>
        <li>Sentences: 2, because the text has two full stops.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Counting diacritics as letters would make the text look eight characters longer than it is.</p>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Why is the count different from Word?</summary><p>Word counts by spaces and may count “و”, numbers or symbols standing alone as separate words. This tool also counts by spaces, but doesn't count punctuation on its own as a word, so the totals can differ slightly.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Do diacritics count?</summary><p>You see the character count with and without diacritics, and the number of diacritics on its own. The word count isn't affected by them.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Is “وقال” one word or two?</summary><p>One, because it is written joined with no space. The tool counts whatever sits between spaces as a word, as most platforms and university word limits do.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Is my text saved?</summary><p>No. Counting happens in your browser and the text is never sent to a server.</p></details>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolPage>
</Layout>
